# XCU fg
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# fg is intrinsic (XCU 1.7). As for bg, the behaviour with job control is
# left optional for a shell that is not interactive, so the positive test
# runs in an interactive shell started with sh -i and reports UNRESOLVED
# when that shell does not have job control enabled.

assertion  XCU.fg.001
anchor     utilities/fg.html#CONSEQUENCES OF ERRORS
anchor     utilities/fg.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       With job control disabled, fg exits greater than zero and puts
           no job into the foreground.
test       t/001-disabled.sh

assertion  XCU.fg.002
anchor     utilities/fg.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/fg.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.11
class      conditional
when       UP
since      1992
says       In an interactive shell with job control, fg moves a background
           job to the foreground, writes its command line and a newline
           to standard output, and the shell waits for the job; afterwards
           the job is gone from the list.
test       t/002-foreground.sh
